Z||000000||donalson||11-10-2001||03:52 AM||||hey guys,<P>a friend and I where discusing the possable engine swaps in the fiero, there are so many options which is a neat thing...me coming from a car that has very few options of rather simple swaps (3 engines if memory serves) anyway we where wondering how much most of you guys paid to do your swaps...did you have a shop do it (sorry thats a sin IMHO) what engine did you swap in? what all extras did you need?<P>i'm talking just the engine swap itself (what it takes to get it drivable) not including supsension upgrades that would be needed to compensate for the weight and such.<P>just cerious   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanks guys<BR>mark<P>------<BR>86 toyota mr2, mid engine lover<p>[This message has been edited by donalson (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||donalson||11-10-2001||04:05 AM||||another thing i'm cerious about...<P>gas milage what kinda gas milage do the respective engines get?...i reber getting 12 in my sisters 85 crown vic LTD...thats something i just can't handel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">...20mpg would be ok i guess though<P>thanks<BR>mark||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||11-10-2001||04:09 AM||||Just for a drivable car?<P>4.6litre 32valve Northstar V8: ~$5,000.00<P>Look on the face of the driver in the Porsche 911 Turbo you just spanked? : Priceless  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: MR2s are neat.  Kind of like Fieros, only reliable...<P>Anything mid-engine rocks!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||donalson||11-10-2001||04:44 AM||||what kinda preformance numbers and weights go w/ these engines?<P>mark||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||11-10-2001||09:45 AM||||You could probably swap a motor for $800-$1000 if you go get a used motor that matches what you had before.  (i.e. not upgrading a 4cyl to a 6cyl)  But if you plan on actually upgrading to something like a Quad 4 or 3.4L or even V-8 you could spend anywhere from $1000-$5000 depending on what you do to your motor before you drop it in the car.<P>A decent (nothing fancy) 3.4L swap could probably done for somewhere around $1200.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dono||11-10-2001||12:02 PM||||Lets see.....$6100 for ZZ4w/TPI and $3100 for Archie conversion kit. Motor not in yet, so thats all I can say.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||11-10-2001||12:25 PM||||An SC3800 can be done for around $5000 but you also get 30 mpg(highway)||||reg||1
Z||000007||GSXPete||11-10-2001||01:57 PM||||are there any kind of archives for engine swaps? i see alot of people asking the same kind of questions concerning swaps, and i think it'd just be alot easier if there was one place with all the info for all known swap, prices, pros/cons, etc. i also had a few questions about the 3800SC. will it bolt up to a 87 gt 5 spd? what else is needed? is it just the cost of the engine that makes it 5 grand? thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroX||11-10-2001||02:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GSXPete:<BR><B>is it just the cost of the engine that makes it 5 grand?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No. I paid $1694 for my engine tranny and wiring harness.  My swap will be completed for less than $3500, thats me doing everything.  check out my website in the next couple months as it develops with my project.  <A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroX.com</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||lowCG||11-10-2001||06:06 PM||||My TDC swap came in at just under $3,000,with a 30K,'97 motor,stainless exhaust;gets 22mpg@100mph.||||reg||1
Z||000010||jelly2m8||11-10-2001||08:00 PM||||MY V8 is totallin approximately 5700.00 canadian.<P>That includes, fresh 350 with TPI, Archie adaptors, the car, a 1985 Fiero GT, grand am brakes at 4 corners, and everything needed to do the conversion, starter waterpump, oil filter adapter, centerforce clutch, 5 spd tranny, exhaust system with resonator tips.<P> This price also includes the 2 used 350's I had in the car.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/P8110011.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/beast.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
